			],
			"Message": "refactor(Maintain): Atomize Build and Eliminate modules into per-function files\n\nSplit the monolithic Source/Build/Process.rs into a Process/ subdirectory with dedicated BuildPlistEnvironment.rs and Process.rs files, extracting the Info.plist LSEnvironment variable collection into its own module for testability and separation of concerns. Split the inline module functions from Source/Build/Rhai/mod.rs into CreateEngine.rs and RegisterUtilityFunctions.rs for a similar per-function structure.\n\nAtomize the Eliminate/Transform module — the 400+ line mod.rs was home to both the span-based Run path and the preserve-layout RunPreserve path with a dozen private helper functions. Each has been extracted to its own file: Run.rs, RunPreserve.rs, PreservePass.rs, TryItemPreserve.rs, TryBlockPreserve.rs, TryPatchSource.rs, CollectBlockPatches.rs, CollectInnerBlockPatches.rs, StmtTokensMatch.rs, StmtToText.rs, and StmtNestedBlock.rs. All private `fn` became pub `fn Fn` accessed via `super::` paths; all call sites (Process.rs, Rhai tests, Eliminate tests in tests/) updated to the new qualified path.\n\nAlso fix the import path in Build/Fn.rs from `crate::Build::Process::Process` to `crate::Build::Process::Process::Fn as Process` reflecting the new module hierarchy, and rewrap prose at 100 chars in Architecture.md.\n\nNo behavioural changes — purely structural modularization.",
			"SHA": "01e27884535a42fac13e6e1ea04d24444b3b37ec"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T22:35:11Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				124,
				1
			],
			"Message": "docs(Maintain): Add Architecture documentation for the build toolkit\n\nAdd a new architecture overview document at Documentation/GitHub/Architecture.md describing the Maintain build toolkit component — its CLI dispatch via clap, cross-element build orchestration, Rhai scripting engine, type-safe TOML/JSON5 config editing, and the build pipeline flow. Also document the Element's deep-shim compatibility tier with the 🟠 orange (Own/Preempt) and 🔵 blue (Proxy/Replace) interception levels, noting that no shim-specific modules exist in Maintain itself — events route through Wind/Mountain/Cocoon.\n\nEstablishes a discoverable entry point for new contributors and cross-references the DeepDive.md doc, BuildPipeline, and Common architecture.",
			"SHA": "085f5fb5e0207a7fa0c4daaeac8f30ef3f6a35c1"
